# The car GLBs copied in for player builds by `npm run sync:unity-cars`
# (scripts/sync-unity-cars.mjs): 17 files, 179 MB of binaries rebuilt
# from press/renders/glb/, which is itself ignored and rebuilt from the
# game. The Editor reads that export directly and never needs the copy.
# The .meta is Unity's, written for the folder the first time it sees it.
/Assets/StreamingAssets/Cars/
/Assets/StreamingAssets/Cars.meta

# The cars baked into Unity assets (Night Racer ▸ Bake Cars to Assets, or
# tools/unity/bake-cars.sh): a prefab per car with its hood, rear window,
# rear wing and tyres as prefabs of their own, plus meshes, materials and
# textures. Generated from the GLBs, several hundred MB under Force Text
# serialization, so baked on each machine rather than committed.
/Assets/Resources/Cars/
/Assets/Resources/Cars.meta

# The studio's scratch (baked probes) — deleted at the end of every render
# run, ignored in case a run is killed first.
/Assets/StudioCache/
/Assets/StudioCache.meta
